### Lab 01 — Serial Interface Troubleshooting

**Case:** CASE-001 Operation Silent Mesh  
**Tool:** Meshtastic CLI 2.7.11  
**Workstation:** Arch Linux  
**Device Interface:** `/dev/ttyACM0`

#### Observations

The Linux workstation identified an Espressif USB JTAG/serial debug interface and assigned it to `/dev/ttyACM0`.

The examiner's account was confirmed to belong to the `uucp` group. Device permissions were `crw-rw----` with ownership `root:uucp`.

The `fuser` command did not identify any process holding the serial interface at the time of examination.

A previous Meshtastic CLI device-information query timed out.

#### Preliminary Assessment

Basic device permissions appear correctly configured. The cause of the Meshtastic communication timeout remains undetermined.

#### Next Investigative Action

Review USB enumeration and serial driver messages. Verify the physical radio model and operating state before conducting another logical acquisition.

**Status:** Troubleshooting ongoing.
